WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.930
&gt;&gt; Malcolm Grant: Good morning, ladies and
gentlemen, and welcome to this meeting of

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:16.139
the Board of NHS England. As you know, we
meet in public, and I am delighted this morning

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:21.390
in London to welcome quite a number of members
of the public. Thank you so much for the interest

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:25.510
that you are taking in our business. Our reason
for meeting in public is that we actually

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:30.800
think that the decisions we take, the debates
that we have and the lead-up to the decisions

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:36.010
are matters of great public interest and affect
the patients, and the public more generally,

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:41.269
of England. You are all very welcome. It is
not a public meeting as such, of course. It

00:00:41.269 --> 00:00:46.559
is a meeting of the Board not only with the
public in the room, but also live streamed

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:49.409
to massive audiences around the world.

00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:55.649
This morning I would particularly like to
welcome a number of students who are studying

00:00:55.649 --> 00:01:01.010
for a master's degree in specialist community
public health nursing. Thank you for coming

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:06.950
this morning, and also for what you are studying,
and for the enormous professional contribution

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:14.550
that you will be able to make to the welfare
of public and patients in your future career.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:21.920
I would also stress that, although we meet
today in public, we do quite a lot of preparatory

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:28.979
work informally. Yesterday we had quite a
lengthy informal session around strategy,

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:33.369
thinking in particular about the financial
position for the NHS in the current year and

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:37.939
the forthcoming spending review, and trying
to understand how this would strategically

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:43.729
affect the business that we would work up
to bring to future meetings of the Board.

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:49.920
Also, because of the way in which the statutory
arrangements are made, we do have formal private

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:55.799
meetings. At the private meetings we take
business which, by reason of confidentiality,

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:04.310
cannot be taken in public. That is a classic
distinction of business for any major public

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:07.069
board.

00:02:07.069 --> 00:02:13.210
Before I go formally into the business of
the meeting, I would like to comment on one

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:19.540
or two changes that are occurring in the Board.
First, there was an announcement recently

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:27.500
by Tim Kelsey, who is our Director of Patients
and Public Information and Engagement, that

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.520
he was to stand down from his role as a director
in order to take up a new post in Australia.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:39.650
He is not with us today, and he tenders his
apologies for the meeting, but I would like

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:48.080
to record our appreciation of his work over
the last four years. This would not have been

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:55.990
his last meeting - he will be with us until
the end of December - but we will shortly

00:02:55.990 --> 00:03:02.790
be recruiting new directors to the Board,
including the successor to Dame Barbara Hakin,

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.610
who is with us this morning.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:11.320
The second thing to note is that this will
be the last meeting of the Board for Ed Smith,

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:16.430
who has been our Deputy Chairman and Chair
of the Audit and Risk Committee. I will say

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:24.610
a few more words about that at the end of
the meeting. In the interim period, whilst

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:31.400
we recruit a new non executive director to
succeed him, I'm happy to report that David

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:36.370
Roberts has agreed to serve as Interim Chair
of the Audit and Risk Committee.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:43.970
I also note that Ciaran Devane, who has been
a member of the Board since the outset, will

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:50.330
stand down at the end of the year upon the
termination of his period of appointment.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:56.410
We will be seeking a fresh appointment to
the Board as his successor. Appointments to

00:03:56.410 --> 00:04:02.600
the Board, by the way, are made by the Secretary
of State, but with the close engagement of

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.970
the Chairman and other members of this Board.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:16.259
Let me then move formally into the business
of the Board. First of all, the apologies

00:04:16.259 --> 00:04:21.509
for absence. We have apologies from Tim Kelsey,
who is travelling abroad with the Secretary

00:04:21.509 --> 00:04:26.880
of State, and from Margaret Casely-Hayford,
who is today chairing a meeting of her own

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.410
board at Action Aid.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:35.380
I invite members of the Board to indicate
whether there are any interests that they

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:40.660
wish to declare in matters arising on the
agenda, above and beyond those already in

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:46.230
our central register. No, there are not.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:55.060
I refer to the minutes of our last meeting,
and ask whether there any comments on the

00:04:55.060 --> 00:05:02.340
minutes and whether the Board happy to accept
them as an accurate report of our last meeting.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:11.150
I find general agreement around the table,
and there are no matters arising that I have

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:11.990
been notified of.

